## When To Update Treaty Docs

At the end of any substantive work session, prepend an entry to `{{ docs_prefix }}work_log.md` and bring `{{ docs_prefix }}next_steps.md` in line with it — unless the user asks you not to document it, says it is off the book, or the exchange was clearly trivial.

The rule that decides what goes in: **the work log records decisions about the project, not the content of the work produced.** The work itself is already in version control; the reasoning behind it is not. See [Work Log Discipline]({{ docs_prefix }}treaty_conventions.md#work-log-discipline) for what counts as substantive, what to skip, and how an entry is structured.

## Branch Handoff Discipline

Before switching away from an experimental or feature branch, fully resolve the work on that branch: confirm it holds all intended changes, that they are committed, and whether the user expects them merged, pushed, or intentionally parked.

Do not switch to the integration branch (`{{ integration_branch }}`) or start new work elsewhere while important experimental-branch changes are only local, unmerged, or unverified. Pre-switch checks and the recovery procedure: [Branch Handoff]({{ docs_prefix }}treaty_conventions.md#branch-handoff).
{% if has_releases %}
## Release / Tag Checklist

Treat any request that combines **commit + push + tag** — or "cut a release" / "publish version X" — as a release. A release has a documentation gate that must clear *before* the tag is created or pushed:

- Version metadata bumped and consistent with the tag.
- Changelog / release notes updated, if this repo has one.
- User-facing docs updated when behavior changed.
- `{{ docs_prefix }}work_log.md` updated with the summary, the verification commands actually run, and the release / branch / tag state, using the verified local date.

Only then create and push the tag, and verify the pushed refs. Full procedure: [Release Gate]({{ docs_prefix }}treaty_conventions.md#release-gate).
{% endif %}
## Updating The Treaty

Pulling upstream treaty refinements into this project is a maintainer's call — only do it when asked, and note it is distinct from updating `{{ docs_prefix }}work_log.md` / `{{ docs_prefix }}next_steps.md` content (above).

`treaty diff` shows this project's section-level drift from the template version it is pinned to; `treaty update --dry-run` previews the merge; `treaty update` applies it as a three-way merge and can leave conflict markers to resolve. Procedure: [Updating The Treaty]({{ docs_prefix }}treaty_conventions.md#updating-the-treaty).

